    "q-118355": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118355",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14256222/assets/2eb034ddf1b9e90dc367d424eaada9a81d2c90f1a6d9727e2352d0308030d5dd.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the graph shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14256222/assets/b9da15e069010f64cbe5a751cab56bbcca985370aaf941b631339e6eb93016f6.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $2.25$ to give $y=-2.25\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-2.25\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
