      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14256222/assets/1970d982fe4a20c1a4384b3a985ebb541056bd71fc5b68496763c0d5bccea3c1.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the graph shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14256222/assets/cc4aa97a9a00cc5ebd332755f3f749b8c387bdf6f60e584489575ec8318a292e.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it across the $x$-axis.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$",
