    "q-118456": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118456",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14256222/assets/f311adf716d9fd0c0c798ec07988837ace5fcfde99ca3bdc2bba277b641b642c.png)\n\nIdentify the equation that generated the graph above.",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14256222/assets/2efc55d4cb4b69db92f1e80760677d432ea947f79871ae481fbbabd63efd2aac.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, translate it by $\\frac{5}{2}$ units **up** to give $y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{5}{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
